caption: Tradition and Mastery Advantages
tradition-component: tradition-and-mastery-advantages

A Style qualifies for a catalog entry when all listed Style prerequisites occur in that same Style. A prerequisite may be one fixed Style Shido, one selected Supernatural Unlock or fixed option, a named Martial Affinity Attribute, or a skill/technique in the Style's mundane source curriculum. An Affinity prerequisite is character-level: the named attribute need only be one of the practitioner's two Martial Affinity Attributes, whether granted by Mundane Martial Art or by Gaoshou, and need not be the Affinity granted by the qualifying Style. All non-Affinity prerequisites still must come from that same Style and cannot be combined across Styles. A Shido prerequisite means it belongs to the Style's fixed package regardless of when it is gained. Tradition Advantages become purchasable at Duan Wei 4 once all prerequisites are actually open; Mastery Advantages additionally require Mastery of the qualifying Style.

Cinematic Skill Expansions [20] take no modifiers and never receive Shido discounts. Other constructions use normal applicable Shido unless stated otherwise.
